# Build-context exclusions for deploy/selfhost/Dockerfile (context = repo root).
#
# Docker does NOT read .gitignore, so before this file existed `COPY . .` baked
# every gitignored thing in the working tree into the image layer -- including
# deploy/selfhost/.env, which holds SECRET_KEY, POSTGRES_PASSWORD and
# DJANGO_CRYPTOGRAPHY_KEY. Those secrets travelled with the image anywhere it was
# saved, exported or pushed to a registry. Compose injects them at RUN time via
# `env_file:`, so the build never needed them.

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Every dotenv shape, examples included: nothing reads them from inside the
# container (compose reads .env on the HOST), so there is no reason to ship them.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- Wrong-platform or rebuilt-anyway artefacts -------------------------------
# .venv is a host (often Windows) virtualenv and useless in a linux image.
# node_modules is reinstalled by `npm ci`; a host copy can carry native binaries
# built for the wrong platform. staticfiles is regenerated by collectstatic --
# shipping a stale copy risks hashed-filename drift against the fresh manifest.
# media is mounted as a named volume at runtime.
.venv/
venv/
node_modules/
staticfiles/
media/

# --- Caches and local scratch -------------------------------------------------
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
*.sqlite3
*.log

# --- Editor / OS ---------------------------------------------------------------
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# NOTE: .git is deliberately NOT ignored.
# scripts/write_build_stamp.py reads it during the build so a plain
# `docker compose build` produces an image that can answer /-/version/ with no
# operator action. It is the whole reason the stamp works zero-touch.
# To slim the image instead, pass the commit explicitly and add `.git` here:
#   GIT_COMMIT=$(git rev-parse HEAD) docker compose -f deploy/selfhost/docker-compose.yml build
